{
  "$comment": [
    "Anywhere Work brand tokens: the single source every user-facing surface derives from.",
    "Surfaces: the desktop client landing page (tools/dsh-netbird/client/index.html), the",
    "Android app (tools/netbird-client/src/theme/tokens.ts), the sign-in page theme",
    "(tools/dsh-netbird/casdoor-theme.sql) and the management console skin",
    "(tools/dsh-netbird/brand/dashboard).",
    "",
    "`type.web.hero` is the landing page's display step. It is 600 rather than the display",
    "step's 700 and carries no tracking, because the page's headline is set in Chinese:",
    "PingFang and Microsoft YaHei smear at 700 on Windows, and a negative letter-spacing that",
    "suits a Latin wordmark squeezes full-width glyphs together. The Latin edition of the page",
    "opts back into tracking in CSS (`html[data-lang='en'] h1`), which is a language rule and",
    "not a size, so it does not belong in the scale.",
    "",
    "The `contrast` array below is the machine-checked part of this file: every pair listed",
    "there is asserted by scripts/dsh-netbird-brand.test.mjs, so a colour cannot be changed",
    "into an inaccessible one without a failing test. Ratios are WCAG 2.x contrast ratios",
    "computed on relative luminance; 4.5 is the AA threshold for body text, 3.0 the AA",
    "threshold for non-text UI (SC 1.4.11) and for focus indicators, 7.0 the AAA threshold",
    "we hold body text to on the surfaces we control.",
    "",
    "Edit this file, then run `node scripts/dsh-netbird-brand.mjs --write` to regenerate the",
    "generated regions in the consumers and `pnpm test:scripts` to re-assert the contract."
  ],

